{"title":"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remark_added_by_not_detriti\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark added by not_detriti</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d53e8788b466db98f427ca777c874e10f2ea1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers such that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca521b92d40def7f320702893c01502439174e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k!=(2^n-1)(2^n-2)(2^n-4)\\dots(2^n-2^{n-1}).\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c924be2d96aaeaadfdfd4b35b06d2a60edb5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />   \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f3103b8c3fbf57974d047791c6dcc81b74cb3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k! = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> (when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e44ca2cae6be42148fe1b1fd8b5d55bd6b599bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f96a3de68cfb881f4b3cc002ec222bba93f1e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d30901de46ae71cd4f0b21eb66e9fc90a2d17c9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RHS = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />(when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />)\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790f46883a296366f038323844601dd2cde9ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb8030c0d8c9e8fb85efd472c1873df6c7e6f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 2: RHS$\" width=\"101\" height=\"12\" /> is strictly increasing, and will never satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> = 2 for integer n since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf50768b010de525677938609e08681d3e1b44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RHS = 6$\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe15ab3fe2677e301243a84519e0cf2bce085008.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k!=(2^n-1)(2^n-2)(2^n-4)\\dots(2^n-2^{n-1})  ...                                                                       (1)\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>In all solutions, for any prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we will denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b50b283b8928a5eddfe5c228ad3d7dad58f03c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_p(N)\\]\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> the exponent of the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The right-hand side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> will be denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/1023c270a3e6299d9db4f0f7860ba6d9f4c67536.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L_n;\\]\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/58616a5783e4d04469be697ef2fd0143e9ed3315.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L_n = (2^n-1)(2^n-2)(2^n-4)\\dots(2^n-2^{n-1})\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d12297fdb0c968bbded8b407d93db3647e9660a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2^{1+2+3+\\dots+(n-1)})(2^n-1)(2^{n-1}-1)(2^{n-2}-1)\\dots(2^1-1)\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456451fe90b72fb25eebe3f7bacbc23c407f8b20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(L_n) = {\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}}\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb4e6a276892ffef24ce71d96dd736e5d548216.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(k!)\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is expressed by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9f09724fda69cb0b5149ef555925b1531f728c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Legendre$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639bca3f0a109995ca19f292fc82846fc4bf6035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$formula$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3766c4a5100a45997f34daff45fea4db5c653fd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(k!) &lt; \\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty} (\\frac{k}{2^i})) = k\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f24e064efae3d0a19b8b3bcd36953ee4925dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k! = L_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> implies the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/196397ae9df44be1f0a28e6c5c7141bdca330d00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} &lt; k    ...                                                   (2)\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />\nIn order to obtain an opposite estimate, observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/58616a5783e4d04469be697ef2fd0143e9ed3315.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L_n = (2^n-1)(2^n-2)(2^n-4)\\dots(2^n-2^{n-1})\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"19\" />\nWe claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd929ebfc430f4d979c962e3b7b3940ed186818.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{n^2} &lt; (\\frac{n(n-1)}{2})!                   ...                                                     (3)\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"38\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d0982bb10a247f1c2a3e3f1b5b5c85b028f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d0982bb10a247f1c2a3e3f1b5b5c85b028f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> the estimate (3) is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f66262261f57a0fe5f69c55585c46eafb976c742.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{6^2} &lt; (6.9)(10^{10})\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"23\" /> \nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eebc618460734b25f3a2e68918eb06ec3862fd9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{n(n-1)}{2})! = 15! &gt; (1.3)(10^{12})\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"38\" />\n~flamewavelight and ~phoenixfire\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Continuing as above, we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3c8361595d2f5129c01792369fb30f7e043e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n &lt; 2^{n^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"23\" />. But this is absurd for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d0982bb10a247f1c2a3e3f1b5b5c85b028f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. So the claim holds. Since we have already checked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f66184ff749c2529112f5154cc5dcf111438ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> it remains to check <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f41bd37c781248db722143858e4f6839aed0ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> and we see neither of them work so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed7b9c811ab2f64be7844a0f4a1f5aab3cf8b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1) and (3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> are the unique two solutions.\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark_added_by_not_detriti\">Remark added by not_detriti</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remark added by not_detriti\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The above solution is very sloppy and no hint is given on how to compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084398a39beca15fe5593f318e432379cf888e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{6^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" /> or where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7d2e9fc8ad9dfc792487f367283f015a5a2603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> comes from. Nevertheless, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be bounded above by observing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/03289968a1f921283b26c5feca9e7f926451c532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n = 2^{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}}(2^n-1)\\cdots(2-1) \\leq 2^{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}} 2^n 2^{n-1} \\cdots 2 = 2^{n(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"488\" height=\"26\" /> whereas, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb7bff6e3b0ec36b17156d943e8691099ed6356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq n(n+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> which we show below, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb523ec91642884ac3a002a1012e9660b9dfa7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k! \\geq \\Big(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\Big)! \\geq 6^{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-5}5! &gt; 6^{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-3}\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"38\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d0982bb10a247f1c2a3e3f1b5b5c85b028f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77207c670d01607594be38c123885f3d7428351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n(n+1)} &gt; L_n \\geq 6^{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"24\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d0982bb10a247f1c2a3e3f1b5b5c85b028f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a2bff6637f34167c1e119a1f1fac1f88f58cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 &gt; 2^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> to simplify this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b20358654357debe33b9706277af032c960bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^3 &gt; 2^{\\frac{n(n+1)}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"22\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a48bb60f5702b968f78d904ac94d88e9fc633a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{\\frac{6\\cdot 7}{4}} &gt; 2^{10} &gt; 6^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a4bbb7a8e48e7d4f767e8626a9e200042d300f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>To show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31d65c516a6aa013519882d187ecae653f8c919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"40\" /> note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d78f13fd8e68d41f8893e52deed3b6cff2d36e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_2(k!) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{k}{2} \\Big\\rfloor + \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{k}{2^2} \\Big\\rfloor + \\cdots \\leq \\frac{k}{2} + \\frac{k}{2^2} + \\cdots = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"383\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO\" title=\"2019 IMO\">2019 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231851\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.086 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 356/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11629/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.067      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.067      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17637:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231851 and revision id 287978. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}